# observed to print (2026-09-29) for three local slash commands sent over
# stream-json with --replay-user-messages, in a fresh session, none of which
# asks the model: no echo of any of them; each turn opens with its init and
# ends with a result of num_turns 0 that names the command (`local_command`).
#
# - `/compact` with nothing to compact: a <synthetic> assistant message that
#   names the command (`local_command_run`), what it printed on stderr, and
#   `local_command_outcome` failed; the result's own text is empty.
# - `/cost`: the command it runs is `usage` (`local_command_run.command`),
#   while the result names `cost`: the name sent is an alias.
# - `/clear`: a `conversation_reset` before the turn's init, and no
#   assistant message at all.
#
# The words printed are made up. "> " is a line DevHub wrote to the CLI's
# stdin (in.log), "< " a line the CLI printed (out), in the order they happened.
